drm: h713: magnify a smaller video picture with proc (letterbox Phase 3)

0161 let the video plane show a picture smaller than the panel, anywhere on
it, at its own size. A 480p or 360p picture therefore stayed a postage stamp
and went to the GPU instead. This lets the plane MAGNIFY such a picture up to
4x per axis through the proc upscaler at 0x05180000, placed anywhere, with
black bars around it. Stock kmssink then letterboxes sub-panel video by
itself: its aspect-fit destination, which the plane used to refuse as a scale,
is now accepted as it stands.

The model is the display firmware's own, extended and hardware-checked in
letterbox Phase 3 (docs/reference/letterbox-recipe-2026-10-04.md "Phase 3:
the scaled model", letterbox-phase1-2026-10-04.md). The table transcribes
tools/display/letterbox-recipe.py, and tools/display/letterbox-kernel-
compare.sh compiles this driver's own table and checks it against the recipe
word for word: 440 words over 11 geometries, all equal.

  - The window layer splits at proc. The SOURCE size runs upstream of it
    (AFBD, the NR line buffers and fetch window, the route source window,
    proc's input window) and the DESTINATION size from its output on (the
    route picture and output windows, the panel video window, the border
    overlay). That is the firmware's split in its one scaled log (720x480 ->
    1280x720).
  - comp+0x858[31:16] is the DESTINATION height. 0161 wrote the source
    height, which is the same thing at unity. Under magnification it starved
    proc after H panel lines and cut every picture at H/ratio source lines
    (bisected on the panel, 2026-10-05).
  - Proc:
      * ratio (in << 16) / out;
      * fractional phases (unity + ratio) >> 2 (H) and >> 1 (V);
      * integer phases 3/2, a unity axis advancing to 4/3;
      * bypass only when both axes are at unity;
      * line-enable length max(in_h, out_h), which was the grey streak of
        2026-09-13;
      * bypass written last.
    The retired chain (0098-0111) had two latent errors here, invisible
    while its destination was always the whole panel. 0111 sized the route
    picture window from the source, and 0108 forced H=3 on a unity axis.
    They are not restored.
  - proc+0x038[31:16] is left alone. The firmware derives it from a member
    it never sets, and its other reading made no visible difference on the
    panel.

The plane gains DRM's SCALING_FILTER property (Default only), the standard
way to say "this plane scales"; h713-play reads its presence to route
sub-panel video to the plane.

At unity every new field reproduces 0161's value, so every geometry 0161
accepted is programmed exactly as before; the probe snapshot check covers the
new scaler words too.

atomic_check now allows a source/destination scale from 1:1 down to 1:4.
DRM counts scale as source over destination, so 4x is the MINIMUM. It refuses:
  - shrinking (the VE's job, at decode time);
  - destinations off the panel;
  - P010 at anything but native size, as before.

The destination's x, width and height are rounded down to even rather than
refused. kmssink centres 852x480 as 1278x720 at x = 1, and on any refusal it
falls back to an unscaled postage stamp. The picture lands at most 1 px from
where it was asked for. 0161 refused an odd x; no unscaled picture kmssink
produces has one.

Verified on the panel before this patch, with the same register values
written from userspace (letterbox-test.sh phase3, 2026-10-05):
  - 640x360 -> 1280x720;
  - 852x480 -> 1278x720;
  - 720x576 -> 960x720 at (160,0);
  - 352x288 -> 880x720 at (200,0);
  - 640x360 -> 960x540 at (160,90).
All were whole and matched reference renders.

